course: dictionary
lesson: 12123
title: Words about fire and feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Combust is a verb. It means to catch fire and burn, especially through a chemical reaction with oxygen. Its forms are combusts, combusted and combusting.
explain: Science gives the clues: «The paper combusted as soon as the match touched it.» A fire needs fuel, heat and oxygen, and the words in the sentence show that the paper caught fire and burned.
explain: Jokes use the word differently. «When Mum saw the muddy footprints, she nearly combusted!» Mum is not on fire. The clue is that she is cross, so combust here means to get very angry or excited.
explain: To check which meaning fits, swap in «catch fire». In «The paper nearly caught fire», the sentence still makes sense as science. In «Mum nearly caught fire», it sounds silly, so the joking meaning is the right one.
fact: Combust means to burn or catch fire, especially through a reaction with oxygen.
fact: Combustion is the noun: it is the process of burning.
fact: A fire needs fuel, heat and oxygen. This is called the fire triangle.
fact: Oily rags and hay can combust on their own if they get hot enough.
fact: In informal speech, «I'll combust!» means I am too angry or excited.
exercise: «The wood combusted in the fireplace.» What does combusted mean? | Cooled down slowly | Turned into water | *Caught fire and burned | Grew bigger
exercise: «Dad nearly combusted when he saw the broken window.» What does nearly combusted mean here? | *Was very angry | Was on fire | Was cold and wet | Was very tired
exercise: Which three things make up the fire triangle? | *Fuel, heat and oxygen | Sugar, salt and flour | Wind, rain and snow | Light, sound and colour
test: Oily rags can combust on their own if they get hot. What does this suggest? | They turn into water | *They can catch fire without a match | They make a loud sound | They freeze when they get cold
test: «I'll combust if you touch my sandwich!» What does the speaker mean? | I'm going to laugh | I'm going to fall asleep | I'm about to catch fire | *I'm about to get very angry
exam: Which word is the noun for the process of burning? | *Combustion | Combusted | Combusts | Combust
